 "words": {
  "rule": "Each side of the street has its own posted sweeping day, one for the odd house numbers and one for the even, most often the 1st and 3rd or the 2nd and 4th time that weekday comes in the month; main streets are swept at night.",
  "afterpass": "All year. A $72 ticket, no tow. No sweeping on City holidays.",
  "dataNotes": "Schedule from Oakland Public Works' street sweeping map (last edited June 21, 2021), the data behind the City's Map Your Street's Sweeping; each side is placed by its house numbers. Checked against 316,353 of the City's street sweeping tickets (January 2025 to July 2026): 73.7% fall in the window shown for that side. On 217 blocks whose tickets show the odd and even days reversed, the two are swapped. 498 sides whose tickets mostly fall outside the posted window are left off the map."
 },
